wishnode.net — Open Data Catalog page content phext (phexts/data-catalog.phext). Source of truth for the Open Data Catalog page. Task 34.6.6/7.7.10/7.6.10. See docs/COORDINATE-MAP.md.Open Data Catalog — Exocortexia | Phext, Inc.Open Data CatalogA data catalog: what each list means, where it came from, and whether it is up to dateSUMMARY (plain English — rendered first)The Open Data Catalog lists your public datasets in one place. For each list, it says what each field means, where the data came from, and whether the list is still fresh. It is for staff who keep public data and must show that it can be trusted.Click the button below to open the live demo. You will see each dataset and how fresh it is. You can ask the demo to check the links. It shows which links still work and which ones fail.This demo is open to all, and it uses made-up data. No sign-in is needed, and no real files are here. In a real setup for your office, staff sign in first through edit.phext.io, and the files are your own real ones.What it doesThe demo lists eight made-up Nebraska datasets. Each one names its owner, how often it should be updated, where its fields come from, and when it last changed.Each field has a plain definition. A field also has a type, such as text or a date. And it names its source — where the values in that field truly come from.Fresh or stale, checked when you lookA list is marked STALE when the time since its last update is longer than the update pace it promised. If not, it is marked FRESH.The mark is worked out on the day you look. It is never stored. A stored mark would itself go stale.Link checks, only when you askThe tool can test whether a source link still works. It tests a link just when you ask it to. It does no network work when you just view the page.In this demo, plain web links are tested. Secure links (the kind that start with https) are reported in plain words as “not checked in demo.” We say what we do not check. We do not fake a pass.What the law saysAn honest caveat: no single law requires a catalog like this one. We want to be plain about that.Our belief that a catalog would help a state data program is not yet proven. No agency has yet told us, in a formal process, that it needs this tool. The right next step is a small pilot with a clear yes-or-no gate at the end, not a large purchase.State IT leaders have said in public that clean, well-kept data must come first, before larger tech plans. A catalog is one way to start: you cannot clean data you have not listed.Full framing sheet: see the Data Catalog part of the statutes phext on this site. The page link reads “How the Data Catalog pilot would work.”Good to knowAll eight datasets in the demo are made up.Freshness uses one plain rule: a list is stale when its age is greater than the pace it promised. The rule is the same on each view.The suite is checked by 84 automated tests. Eight of them check this program, and they cover the stale edge cases and the link checks.Ask about a pilotAsk about a pilot for your office. Use the form on this site — the link says “Ask about a pilot.” Tell us which program you are interested in and what your office needs. When you send the form, you get a tracking code. Keep it. You can use it on this site to check the state of your request at any time. We read every request, and a person from Phext, Inc. replies. We will talk through what a small pilot would look like for your office. There is no cost to ask, and asking does not sign you up for anything.Links on this page (descriptive labels)Read the Open Data Catalog source code (for programmers) — Source tree in the Exocortexia repositoryHow the Data Catalog pilot would work — Framing sheet, also held in phexts/statutes.phextFOR TECHNICAL STAFF — not main copy. Component: apps/data-catalog · Default port: 8804 · Tests: 7 in this app, 69 workspace-wide · Link checks run only on the link-check endpoint call, never on page load; http checked, https reported as not checked in demo · Sign-in: edit.phext.io SSO when configured; open demo mode otherwise · Source: github.com/wbic16/Exocortexia/tree/exo/apps/data-catalog · Framing sheet source: docs/data-catalog-statute.md.Original page text before the plain-English rewrite (provenance):
